<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL RAISES GASOLINE PRICES BY TWO CENTS.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL RAISES GASOLINE PRICES BY TWO CENTS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit</p>
<p>Shell Nederland BV said on Friday it would raise its retail</p>
<p>prices for gasoline in the Netherlands by two cents per litre</p>
<p>with effect from Monday, July 28.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices</p>
<p>and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company</p>
<p>said. It added diesel prices would remain unchanged.</p>
<p>From Monday the price of premium unleaded gasoline at</p>
<p>Shell's self-service stations will rise to 2.26 guilders per</p>
<p>litre. The price of premium with lead substitute goes up to 2.33</p>
<p>guilders and Euro regular unleaded to 2.21 guilders.</p>
<p>The recommended price for diesel remains at 1.516 guilders</p>
<p>per litre, Shell said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
